  "notes": "Mapping v3 (owner-reviewed 2026-10-12; docs/model-tier-mapping-2026-10-12.md). Equivalence by capability class, not price. Model ids and billing follow the canonical catalog (config/models.json) via catalog_provider; tests enforce it. plan=included is an OAuth/plan route. plan=metered with declarable_included is a route that is paid by default and becomes an automatic included route only where an owner declares the plan includes usage (request included_plans): GLM (direct API, max coding plan; key from Google Secret Manager on the VPN) and Gemini Flash (Gemini CLI; OAuth plus GCP IAM, a plan for entitled users). A live probe per user decides whether the declared plan is actually reachable. glm-hosted is the hosted coding-plan route: unverified, pin-only. Paid API-key native routes are not in the table: paid models are reached through OpenRouter only. probe_required: Gemini Flash is only automatic with a successful live probe for the user (OAuth plus GCP IAM, from an allowed IP), never from a declaration alone; a pin is unaffected. Devin's Gemini and Grok models are billable at the model level in the catalog (only the swe-* models are included in the Devin plan), so they are not in this table: paid models are reached through OpenRouter only. Devin therefore has no low-tier model.",
